Hehe, I've had the same problem now you mention this... :-)

It was on an Alpha DS25, with 3 PSU's.
After a shutdown I removed them to clean them a bit with pressured air, 
and later the system would not boot either, it just did nothing, and 
there were no lights either.

After some panicing we saw that the PSU's were also not seated deep 
enough, you really have too press hard, even securing them with the 
screw did not work (since the screw-secured levers were not touching 
anything).

As you can see, most people never follow the checklists in such a 
problem, we always think it's something worse ;-p

Wimmy


